  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The distance of the centre <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the line <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units which is greater than the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math><br />Therefore,&nbsp;the line is neither tangent nor secant to the circle</p><p>Hence, nearest point P on the line from the circle is the foot of the perpendicular from the centre on the&nbsp;line.<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> If <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then</p><p><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math> &amp; <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
